                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": 2784150,
            "level": 1,
            "value": "Of course, hard work is valuable, but only when properly targeted. Otherwise, it wastes the resources that companies value most, time and energy, and that's bad for the organization. There's a management model that groups people according to four criteria, clever, hardworking, stupid, and lazy. Here, lazy means having a rational determination not to carry out unnecessary tasks. It doesn't mean trying to avoid work altogether.",
            "children": [
              {
                "id": 2784151,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Of course, hard work is valuable, but only when properly targeted.",
                "meta": {
                  "to": 266.67,
                  "from": 262.27002,
                  "speaker": "Speaker 2"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": 2784163,
                "level": 2,
                "value": "Otherwise, it wastes the resources that companies value most, time and energy, and that's bad for the organization.",
